  "swiftAnchor": "leanring-buddy/CompanionManager.swift:430-756",
  "description": "Seam 6. Document swiftAnchor is the primary CompanionManager state-machine range; additional anchors (CompanionManager.swift:175-195 keyterms; CompanionPanelView.swift:128-130, 728-759 panel status) live on the cases they justify. Cases without a group start from CompanionSessionState.Initial (isClickyCursorEnabled true, overlay hidden, plus input.initialHistory when present) and feed input.events to CompanionSession.Reduce in order on a virtual clock. Event types: started {isClickyCursorEnabled, hasCompletedOnboarding, hasMicrophonePermission}, shortcutPressed, shortcutReleased, recordingStarted, transcriptFinal {text}, responseReady {requestId, text}, responseFailed {requestId, error}, ttsStarted, ttsEnded, pointingFinished, and advance {ms}, which moves the clock and reduces a transientHideElapsed for every scheduleTransientHide timer that came due. expected.voiceStates and expected.effects have one entry per event (the state after it, and the effects it emitted, in order); expected.history is the conversation history after the last event. Effects are written as 'showOverlay', 'hideOverlay', 'scheduleTransientHide <id> <delay>ms', 'dismissPanel', 'cancelChatRequest <id>', 'stopTtsPlayback', 'clearPointingTarget', 'startRecording', 'stopRecording', 'startChatRequest <id> history=<count>', 'pointAtElement <x>,<y> <label>', 'speakResponse <text>', 'speakFallbackUtterance <text>' and 'analytics <event name>[: <content>]'. Cases in group panel-status feed input {hasCompletedOnboarding, hasMicrophonePermission, isOverlayVisible} with each voiceState to CompanionPanelStatus.From; expected.byVoiceState gives statusText and dotColor (a DS colour token) per voiceState, and expected.hintText the push-to-talk hint (null when the panel shows setup copy instead). Parity spec PTT-02, PTT-03, CLA-06, CLA-07, AN-02, TTS-02, ONB-03, PNL-06.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "full-exchange-with-point",
